    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-28T04:10:53+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-28T04:10:53+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-27T18:40:53Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-27T18:40:53Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough over central Australia will weaken and contract into WA as a ridge of high pressure extends across southeastern SA. The high pressure system is expected to drift into the Tasman Sea by Tuesday as the trough in WA begins to re-extend over western SA on Tuesday, pushing into the state on Wednesday and reaching the far northeast on Thursday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-28T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-29T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-27T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-28T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west this evening. Winds north to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures in the mid to high 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 3:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-29T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-30T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-28T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-29T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers in the far west, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the evening. Winds northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h in the early morning then tending southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-30T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-01T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-29T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-30T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers in the far west, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northeast to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northwesterly during the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 28 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-01T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-30T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm. Light winds becoming south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending south to southeasterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 23 to 31.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
